            <ArticleTitle>Unexplained high activity of aspartate aminotransferase (EC 2.6.1.1): a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>224-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of unexplained and persistently elevated ASAT activity in serum. This appeared to be due to a macro-enzyme of ASAT, as was demonstrated by protein-A-Sepharose treatment of the serum sample. Although macro-ASAT seems to be clinically irrelevant, unexplained raised ASAT activity without acknowledgement of its macroenzyme nature may lead to unnecessary diagnostic procedures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
